      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "70516cce-49d8-4d2f-a4cf-0757b4629826",
              "name": "chatInput",
              "value": "=Today is {{ $now.format('cccc, dd LLLL yyyy') }} and the time is {{ $now.format('HH:mm') }} ({{ $now.zoneName }}).\n\nPrepare my daily briefing. Use your tools to collect real data. Do not guess or invent anything. Write in a professional, courteous and concise tone.\n\n1) EMAILS - Search my unread emails from the last 24 hours (since {{ $now.minus({ hours: 24 }).toISO() }}) using the Gmail search query: is:unread newer_than:1d -category:promotions -category:social. Sort them from OLDEST to NEWEST by the date and time they were sent, so the most recent unread email appears last. For each email provide:\n- Sender: the sender's name only (no email address)\n- Subject\n- Sent: date and time in my local timezone, formatted like \"20 Oct 2026, 14:35\"\n- Summary: one short sentence\nIf there are no emails, write only: \"No unread emails from the last 24 hours.\" and nothing else in this section.\n\n2. EVENTS - Get all my calendar events today. List them in chronological order, showing the event name, time slot, and location if available. Use exactly these formats:\n\n* Event Name - HH:MM - HH:MM - Location: Event Location\n* Event Name - HH:MM - HH:MM\n* All-day Event Name - All day\n\nInclude the location exactly as provided by Google Calendar. If no location is available, omit the entire \" - Location: ...\" portion. For timed events, use 24-hour time in HH:MM format. For all-day events, use \"All day\" instead of a time slot. Do not mention attendees, overlaps or free time. If there are no events, write only: \"No events for today.\"\n\n3) TASKS - Get my open (not completed) tasks that are due today or overdue. List them in order of due date, showing the task name, due date when available, and due time if available. Preserve the task's due time when one exists; do not invent a time if none is provided. Format examples:\n- Submit report - Due: 20 Oct 2026, 14:30\n- Review document - Due: 20 Oct 2026\n\nTreat a due date as a calendar date when determining whether a task is due today or overdue, so a task due today is not overdue just because its time has passed. If there are no tasks, write only: \"No tasks today.\"\n\nRules: This is read-only. Do not send emails, create drafts, or change or delete any event or task. Do not add a summary, priorities, recommendations or any extra commentary. If a tool fails, state which one in a single sentence. Format as plain text with the section headings EMAILS, EVENTS and TASKS in capital letters, hyphen bullets for events and tasks, and no markdown symbols such as ** or #. Begin the response with the line: Daily Briefing - {{ $now.format('dd LLL yyyy') }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
